# firmware/ is ALL build output, not source: the sdcard image (~3 GB),
# kernels, DTBs, U-Boot. Every one is reproducible with scripts/build.sh.
# Git stores a full copy of every changed binary, so tracking these would add
# gigabytes per rebuild (the reference project learned this the hard way).
/firmware/

# ROM archives: large, regenerable, and not ours to distribute.
backup/

# Scratch
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej

# NOTE: buildroot-external/package/retroarch/retroarch/retro-assets IS tracked
# deliberately -- retroarch.mk copies it into the target, so it is a build
# input, not an output.

# Cover art fetched by scripts/fetch-thumbnails.py (publishers' artwork, never committed)
scripts/thumbnails-cache/

# Slot-10 save states, the game tests' start points (scripts/game-test.sh),
# copied from the boards' cards: game memory snapshots of the user's games,
# 1-12 MB each (compressed). Kept here to restore or copy to another card,
# never committed. scripts/fetch-test-states.sh <board> fills it.
test-states/
